error[resolve.receiver]: `self` names a method's receiver — a default is a body of its own, and has none
  ╭─[<case>/src/main.av:3:19]
3 │     fn m(k: int = self.x) -> int { k }
  ·                   ┬
  ·                   ╰── no receiver here
──╯
help: let the seat default to absence and fill it in the body — `k: int? = null`, then `k ?? self.x`
